BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:LiveMusicAsheville.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260417
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260419
DTSTAMP:20260417T230455
CREATED:20260417T141658Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T141658Z
UID:10057812-1776394800-1776481199@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:COMING Next Saturday\, April 25 | Pisgah Palooza 2026 - (21 Years of Pisgah Brewing)
DESCRIPTION:Saturday April 25\, 2026 6:00 PM | Doors Open: 5:00 PM | Advance Tickets are on sale now – 2 for $21! Event Details and Tickets\n\nJoin us on April 25th to celebrate 21 years of Pisgah Brewing with Sqwerv\, Airshow and Pocketful of Gold.\n\nDenver’s electrifying Indie-Jam Band\, Sqwerv is a nationally touring quartet that brings elements of classic rock\, psychedelic music\, funk\, and jam fusion for an experience like no other. The band explores rich sonic realms with a depth of improvisational virtuosity. Their passion for well crafted songs and blended harmonies set this group apart in their scene. The band released 2 full length studio albums in 2024\, ‘Mirage’ and ‘Hors d’Oeuvres’ and has a new full length record on the way in 2025. They have opened for acts such as George Clinton and Parliament Funkadelic\, Pigeons Playing Ping Pong\, Eggy\, Big Something\, Spafford and many more.\n–\nAirshow is a high-flying\, Nashville-based jam band featuring a unique contrast of familiar acoustic and mind-bending electric sounds that transports listeners from a campfire picking-party to the outer reaches of the multiverse. Formed by longtime friends Cody Chelius (Mandolin / Vocals) and Steve Gallagher (Guitar / Vocals)\, the group’s lineup was completed with the addition of Bill Baker (Bass/ Vocals) and John Rodrigue (Drums/ Vocals) in 2016. While each member has different musical influences\, it is their shared passion for exploring uncharted sonic territories that has propelled their ascension to the top of Nashville’s jamband scene— and they won’t be landing anytime soon.\n–\nPocketful of Gold\, Asheville’s newest Led Zeppelin Experience\, makes their debut on Pisgah’s Outdoor Stage! Featuring Hannah Ramsey\, Alex Bazemore\, Jackson Chisholm\, and Zach Jones\, these frizzy-haired folk bring their love of Led Zeppelin together to offer a musical experience that both honors their iconic sound and showcases the inspiration that it’s had on each member’s personal musicianship.\n  \nFounded in 2005\, Pisgah is known for producing some of the most sought after craft ales in Western North Carolina. Pisgah Brewing Company currently operates the new indoor taproom & deli\, with live music several days a week\, plus an open air outdoor bar in the summer and fall months. Check out our upcoming schedule at pisgahbrewing.com/events
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/coming-next-saturday-april-25-pisgah-palooza-2026-21-years-of-pisgah-brewing/
LOCATION:Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain\, 2948 US-70\, Black Mountain\, NC\, 28711
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Black Mountain,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/617704239_1358962522924587_2721723407800321272_n-e1769530924423.jpg
GEO:35.6068069;-82.3568213
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain 2948 US-70 Black Mountain NC 28711;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2948 US-70:geo:-82.3568213,35.6068069
END:VEVENT
